10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
The Polar Express is a 2004 American animated Christmas fantasy adventure film directed by Robert Zemeckis, who co-wrote the
screenplay with William Broyles Jr., based on the 1985 children's book of the same name by Chris Van Allsburg.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
The film stars Tom Hanks in multiple roles, along with Daryl
Sabara, Nona Gaye, Jimmy Bennett, and Eddie Deezen.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The film depicts human characters using live action and motion capture computer animation, with
production sequences for the latter taking place from June 2003 to May 2004.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Set on Christmas Eve, it tells the story of a young boy who travels to the
North Pole aboard a magical train guided by its conductor.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The Polar Express premiered at the Chicago International Film Festival on
October 13, 2004, and was theatrically released by Warner Bros.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Pictures in the United States on November 10.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and initially grossed $286 million against a
record-breaking $165–170 million budget, which was the highest for an animated feature at the time.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Later re-releases helped propel the film's gross to $318.2 million worldwide.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film explores themes of faith, holiday, santa claus, nerd, bell.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The tone is lighthearted.
